Lakṣmaṇa enters Suyajña's house at Rāma command --- Suyajña worships twilight and enters shining Rāma house --- Rāma with Sītā honors Suyajña with gold gems and couch --- Rāma gives jewels for wife and elephant Śatruṃjaya worth a thousand --- Suyajña accepts and blesses Rāma Lakṣmaṇa Sītā --- Rāma bids honor Agastya Kauśika and reward long-serving Citraratha --- Rāma bids grant palanquin slave-girls silks to Taittirīya teacher, cattle to others --- Lakṣmaṇa distributes wealth like Kubera keeping houses for return --- Rāma gives wealth to young old brāhmaṇas needy through treasurer --- Poor gleaner Trijaṭa Gārgya begs favor, hurls staff, wins cattle herd as jest
